<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item>3.2.1: Selecting the Best Line</item>
  <item>3.2.2: Determining the Best Line That Fits the Data<list>
      <item>3.2.2: Self Check </item>
      <item>3.2.2: Additional Resources </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>3.2.3: Writing Linear Models without Technology
    <list>
      <item>3.2.3: Self Check </item>
      <item>3.2.3: Additional Resources </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>3.2.4: Assessing the Fit of a Linear Model
    <list>
      <item>3.2.4: Self Check </item>
      <item>3.2.4: Additional Resources </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>3.2.5: Working with Fitted Lines</item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 3.2.6: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list>
  <item>Graphing technology</item>
  <item><link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/be91d7ce246445302f3baee0c36286ebea6c2034">Activity 3.2.2 card sort</link> blackline masters</item>
  <item>Coordinate grids</item>
</list>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<para>Print and cut up slips for the <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1a32fc7619feae137f83a8a58369c908593bb1d8">card sort.</link> Prepare one copy of the blackline master for every group of 2 students. To find best
  fit lines, students will need access to technology that will compute the least-squares regression lines for a set of
  data.</para>
<para>Acquire devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology. It is ideal if each student has their
  own device. </para>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look for
    these words and notice their use and meanings.</item>
  <item>Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral explanations.
  </item>
  <item>Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link></item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
